  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="commodity_dudgeon_cb19c5b66f3b779f938bdc75e6e1703bb3b30a5de8ae835b2ff8a7cf870f0137f2c">
    <crm:P190_has_symbolic_content>a kind of hardwood (perhaps boxwood), used by turners, especially for handles of knives, daggers etc.; the hilt of a dagger made from this wood (OED s.v. dudgeon n.1) | a kind of hardwood (perhaps boxwood), u.a. used by turners, especially for handles of knives, daggers etc.; the hilt of a dagger made from this wood (OED s.v. dudgeon n.1) | a kind of hardwood (perhaps boxwood), among other things used by turners, especially for handles of knives, daggers etc.; the hilt of a dagger made from this wood (OED s.v. dudgeon n.1) | a kind of hardwood (perhaps boxwood), used by turners, especially for handles of knives, daggers etc. (OED s.v. dudgeon n.1) | a kind of hardwood (perhaps boxwood), u.a. used by turners, especially for handles of knives, daggers etc. (OED s.v. dudgeon n.1) | (dougeon) a kind of hardwood (perhaps boxwood), u.a. used by turners, especially for handles of knives, daggers etc.; the hilt of a dagger made from this wood (OED s.v. dudgeon n.^1) | a kind of hardwood (perhaps boxwood), among other things used by turners, especially for handles of knives, daggers etc. (OED s.v. dudgeon n.1) | a kind of hardwood (perhaps boxwood), u.a. used by turners, especially for handles of knives, daggers etc. (OED s.v. dudgeon n.^1) | a kind of hardwood (perhaps boxwood), used by turners, esp. for handles of knives, daggers etc.; the hilt of a dagger made from this wood (OED s.v. dudgeon n.1)</crm:P190_has_symbolic_content>
    <crm:P2_has_type rdf:resource="http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435416"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E33_Linguistic_Object"/>
  </rdf:Description>
